    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan made. Recombinant zoster vaccine dose 1, PCV20 and Tdap given. Mammography, cervical screening, colorectal screening by stool test, and HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening ordered. Bone density measured three weeks ago. Lipid screening deferred until weight is restored, because starvation distorts the result. [S]<list><item>Second zoster vaccine dose in two to six months.</item><item>Mammogram and cervical screening booked at the women&apos;s health clinic, in a private appointment.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Anorexia nervosa, restricting type (F50.011)</content>. Weight 50.4 kg, BMI 17.0, gaining; pulse 58. [S]<list><item>Continue the team plan; next eating disorder review as booked.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Recurrent depression with persistent grief (F33.1)</content>. PHQ-9 13, early on sertraline 50 mg; passive thoughts less often, no intent or plan. [S]<list><item>Safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>100/64 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 13 on treatment; followed in her depression care</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No alcohol</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Biennial mammography from 40 to 74; ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>HPV testing every five years from 30 to 65; no record of recent screening; ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Due from 45; she chose a yearly fecal immunochemical test; kit given</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>DXA three weeks ago for a postmenopausal woman under 65 at increased risk: low bone mass</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Due</td><td>Due; postponed until weight is restored, because starvation can raise cholesterol; to be checked at the next preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not overweight; glucose followed in her eating disorder care</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 15 to 65; drawn today with her agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test for adults 18 to 79; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine dose 1 of 2 today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 today; recommended for all adults 50 or older</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap today</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>In the autumn</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine (PCV20); Tdap vaccine [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: The American Psychiatric Association Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Eating Disorders, Fourth Edition (2023); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Twelve-week eating disorder review in five weeks. Screening results through the patient portal, which is set to private. Next scheduled visit 2026-04-28: twelve-week review: weight restoration, exercise, mood and sertraline. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

